              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕನ್ನಡಕ (kannaḍaka) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil kaṇṇāṭi (DEDR 1182). DEDR lists kanaḍaka, \"pair of spectacles\", beside kannaḍi, \"mirror, lens\". The entry explains the Tamil word as kaṇ, \"eye\", with āṭi, \"mirror\"."
            }
